  "summary_en": "European Commission's 2021 proposal replacing the Machinery Directive 2006/42/EC with a directly applicable Regulation. It adds requirements for new digital technologies (cobots, AI, software updates, cybersecurity, autonomous machines), mandates third-party conformity assessment for high-risk machinery including AI safety software, introduces substantial-modification rules, and coordinates with the AI Act.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Converts Machinery Directive into a Regulation aligned with the New Legislative Framework",
   "High-risk machinery (Annex I, including AI safety-function software) requires notified-body third-party conformity assessment",
   "Substantial modification by physical or digital means makes the modifier a manufacturer needing new conformity assessment",
   "Safety components include software; risk assessment must cover evolving autonomous behaviour and cybersecurity of control systems",
   "Machinery with AI systems: AI Act requirements checked within machinery conformity assessment; Regulation covers safe integration only"
  ],
